  "status": "published",
  "title": "Pipe Desk Lamp",
  "summary": "A jointed desk lamp built from black iron fittings. Wire through the pipe for a tidy finish.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 2,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Black iron fittings come coated in oil. Scrub every piece with mineral spirits and a rag, inside and out, then let them dry.",
    "Dry-assemble the lamp in this order: floor flange, 6 in nipple, elbow, 8 in nipple, elbow, 8 in nipple, cap. Hand-tighten only, so you can adjust the pose later.",
    "Drill a 7/16 in hole in the centre of the pipe cap with the step bit. Push the 1/8 IP lamp pipe through, with a locknut on each side, and tighten.",
    "Drill a 1/2 in hole in the 6 in nipple, 1 in above the flange, and press in a rubber grommet so the cord cannot chafe on the cut edge.",
    "Unscrew the cap. Feed the cord in through the grommet and fish it up through every fitting and out through the lamp pipe. A length of stiff wire taped to the cord end makes the bends easier.",
    "Thread the socket cap onto the lamp pipe. Split the cord about 3 in and tie an underwriter's knot. Strip 1/2 in from each conductor. Connect the ribbed (neutral) conductor to the silver screw and the smooth conductor to the brass screw. Snap the socket shell closed.",
    "Screw the cap back on. Tighten the joints with the pipe wrench until the lamp holds its pose. Spray two light coats of clear lacquer to stop rust.",
    "Fit the bulb and test the inline switch. If the lamp tips when the arm is extended, screw the flange to a hardwood base."
  ],
